---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { absoluteUrl, isCommodityNode } from '../lib/site-variant';

if (!isCommodityNode) return Astro.redirect('/blog/');
const canonicalUrl = absoluteUrl('/developers/');
---

<Base
  title="Developers"
  metaTitle="CommodityNode Developer Access"
  description="Read-only CommodityNode MCP tools, public graph endpoint, identifiers, evidence limits, and current access boundaries."
  canonicalUrl={canonicalUrl}
>
  <article class="static-page prose">
    <p class="section-label">Developer access</p>
    <h1>Query the published graph without losing its evidence boundaries.</h1>
    <p class="article-dek">
      CommodityNode exposes reviewed records for inspection and integration.
      Draft editorial data, fixtures, private lead records, saved items, and
      account alerts are not part of the public data surface.
    </p>

    <h2>Model Context Protocol</h2>
    <p>
      The MCP endpoint is <code>https://commoditynode.com/mcp</code>. Four
      CommodityNode tools are read-only and idempotent:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>commoditynode_list_events</code> — published Event Pulse records.</li>
      <li><code>commoditynode_list_benchmarks</code> — benchmarks, proxies, and named relationships.</li>
      <li><code>commoditynode_list_routes</code> — reviewed route-reference records.</li>
      <li><code>commoditynode_get_evidence</code> — one entity, edge, or evidence record.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Route status is registry metadata, not vessel telemetry. Relationship edges
      identify an analytical connection, not a price forecast.
    </p>

    <h2>Public graph endpoint</h2>
    <p>
      <code>/api/commoditynode-graph</code> supports the bounded operations
      <code>snapshot</code>, <code>resolve</code>, <code>subgraph</code>,
      <code>path</code>, and <code>evidence</code>. Text parameters are limited
      to 160 characters; hop, node, and edge limits are clamped by the graph
      service. Responses include only the published snapshot.
    </p>
    <pre><code>GET /api/commoditynode-graph?op=evidence&amp;id=evidence-panama-court-law-406</code></pre>

    <h2>Identifiers and versioning</h2>
    <p>
      Commodity, route, event, entity, edge, evidence, snapshot, and ontology
      identifiers are stable within a published version. Consumers should store
      the snapshot ID and ontology version with derived work. A correction may
      supersede a claim without rewriting the historical publication record.
    </p>

    <h2>Keys and paid scopes</h2>
    <p>
      CommodityNode API keys and paid scopes are not for sale. The candidate
      contract defines history, export, and advanced-path scopes, but none is
      advertised as available until feature, legal, privacy, support, and payment
      reconciliation gates all pass.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a
        href="/brief/"
        data-commoditynode-event="api_docs_opened"
        data-commoditynode-placement="developers_brief"
        data-commoditynode-conversion="api"
      >Discuss a bounded integration or data brief</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
